# Reuse existing engines first

When adding or fixing an interactive exercise (match, cloze, hunt, flip, gaps, Live, sticky rail, writing studio, etc.):

## Mandatory order

1. **Search the repo first** (`*-engine.js`, etalon pages, committed Listening Part 3 pages).
2. **Reuse** that engine + CSS + markup. New **content/data** only.
3. Invent a one-off UI **only** if nothing fits — say so briefly.

## HARD RULE — Listening Part 3 / speakers ↔ A–H

**Do NOT** convert Listening Part 3 to `FCE_SENTENCE_HALVES_MATCH` / drag chips / “Not used” seat rows.

| ✅ Required (exam paper style) | ❌ Forbidden for Listening Part 3 |
|--------------------------------|-----------------------------------|
| Static **Options A–H** list (full sentences) on the left | SHM two-column seat/swap UI |
| **Speakers 1–5** on the right with `<select>` letter choices | Parking spare letters on “Not used” rows |
| Letter uniqueness (used letter disappears from other selects) | Replacing the classic select engine “for consistency” |

**Etalons (restore from git if mangled):**

1. `unit1-listening/sb-1-1/part3-multiple-matching.html`
2. `listening/unit10/fce/telling-lies/part3-multiple-matching.html` (keeps Evidence hunt)
3. `unit1-listening/wb-moving-country/` — same select pattern for Ex. 1 / 2 / 4

**Compact UI:** shared `css/fce-listening-part3-select.css` (`.fce-p3-split` / `.fce-p3-panel` / `.fce-p3-opt` / `.fce-p3-row`). Dense rows, no stretch gaps. Use `--wide` when options are full A–H sentences.

## Sentence-halves SHM (vocab / grammar / some writing)

Use `FCE_SENTENCE_HALVES_MATCH` **only** for beginnings↔endings style tasks (give-collocations, reporting-verbs, article purposes, etc.) — see `fce-sentence-halves-match-opposite.mdc`.

**Not** for Listening Part 3 speaker matching.

## HARD RULE — FCE Reading Part 6 / gapped text (A–G sentences)

**Do NOT** put `<select>` dropdowns inside the passage or use a single-column “bank above text” layout.

| ✅ Required (Honesty / Capoeira split) | ❌ Forbidden for Part 6 gapped text |
|----------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|
| Split pane: passage **left**, options + **Your answers** **right** | Inline selects in the article |
| Numbered gap **chips** only in text (`{{1}}` → square `1`) | SHM / drag chips / custom one-off JS per unit |
| Right rail: A–G list + `— choose —` dropdowns per gap | Listening Part 3 `.fce-p3-opt` bank-above-text pattern |

**Etalons:** `unit10-reading-honesty-is-the-best-policy/`, `unit2-reading/joys-of-capoeira/`, `unit7-reading-black-friday/`.

**Engine:** `js/fce-reading-part6-gapped.js` + `css/fce-reading-part6-gapped.css` + `FCE_R6_PACK` data — see `fce-reading-part6-gapped-split.mdc`.

